Fix pre-release review findings: data loss, stuck state, wrong results

A three-way review sweep of the data, UI and search layers found 31 real
problems. This fixes the crash, data-loss and wrong-behaviour ones. Each was
reproduced before being fixed — ReviewFindingsTest holds the reproductions for
the three that are pure logic, and 8 of its 10 assertions failed before these
changes.

DATA LOSS

The composer had no BackHandler, so the system back gesture bypassed
onLeaveComposer entirely. Text typed inside the 3s autosave window was lost
outright, and an autosaved Memory stayed in DRAFT — never enqueued, never
enriched, never searchable. Back is how most people leave a screen, so this was
the likeliest way to lose content in the whole app.

Removing an attached image dropped the path but left the canonical image and its
thumbnail on disk with nothing referencing them.

STUCK STATE

A Memory could be stranded in PROCESSING permanently. The state was written
before the first stage and was not an eligible entry state, so a worker killed
mid-run — process death, or WorkManager stopping it on low battery — left the
Memory claimed by a run that no longer existed. The retry saw PROCESSING,
returned NotEligible, and the worker reported that as success. markFailed was
unreachable, retryProcessing refuses anything but FAILED, and nothing swept
stale rows. The card span forever with no way back short of clearing app data.

Fixed three ways: PROCESSING is now an eligible entry state with a
self-transition so an interrupted run resumes; StaleProcessingSweeper releases
Memories older than 15 minutes at startup so the user gets the retry
affordance; and CancellationException is rethrown rather than swallowed in both
the pipeline and the worker, with the terminal markFailed write made
NonCancellable so it cannot be lost during teardown.

EVERY AI FEATURE SILENTLY DID NOTHING IN THE BACKGROUND

ProviderManager held the active provider in memory only, and nothing but the
onboarding and settings screens ever set it. Enrichment runs in a WorkManager
worker that Android usually starts in a fresh process, where no screen has run —
so summarisation, categorisation, metadata extraction and vision all found no
provider and recorded NOT_SUPPORTED, while Settings showed the provider as
correctly configured. ProviderRestorer now restores it at application start and
before each worker run.

The one method that could have restored it, getCloudConfig, collected
DataStore.data — an infinite flow — instead of taking first(), so it never
returned. It had no callers, which is the only reason that had gone unnoticed.

Settings "Test" mutated the live provider: a mistyped key replaced a working
provider with a broken one, or on the failure branch left none at all, while the
screen still displayed the old one as current. Testing now uses a throwaway
provider. Separately, onConfirmCloudConfig only persisted and never activated,
so a user who skipped Test saved a config that did nothing until next launch.

WRONG RESULTS

Bare month names became hard date filters. "the ramen recipe I may have saved"
restricted results to the whole of last May and reported "No memories found"
with nothing to explain it. The preposition is now required.

FtsQuery kept dots inside terms while SQLite's simple tokeniser splits on them,
so a query for "js" matched a document containing "node.js" in FTS and then
scored zero against the term "node.js" and was discarded — verbatim the failure
KeywordScoring's own docstring forbids. Reachable with js, png, pdf, kt, com.

Deleting a Memory left its FTS row behind. memory_search_index is an FTS4
virtual table and SQLite supports no foreign keys on virtual tables, so unlike
all ten relational child tables it does not cascade. Deleted text stayed
matchable and occupied slots inside the query LIMIT.

Temporal parsing sliced the original query using offsets computed on its
lowercased copy. Lowercasing is not length-preserving — U+0130 becomes two
characters — so "İSTANBUL trip last week" threw
StringIndexOutOfBoundsException into an unguarded viewModelScope.launch. A
crash while typing.

isSearchActive keyed on raw text while results came from FtsQuery.build, which
returns null for single characters and stopword-only queries. Typing "the" or
"a" showed a hard "No memories found".

IN (:ids) was unbounded. Room binds one parameter per id and SQLite on API 30 —
this app's floor — caps them at 999, so the feed would fail outright at a
thousand Memories. Now chunked.

Onboarding "Retry" was permanently inert: it routed to onStartDownload, which
returns immediately when no generative model is selected, and since local
inference is deferred (ADR-0002) there never is one. Users hit a frozen 0%
screen whose only exit was Cancel. The same null made the header read
"Downloading " with a blank name for everyone.

Notification deep links destroyed all UI state on every tap and re-fired on
rotation. onNewIntent only called setIntent, which nothing observes, so a tap at
a live Activity could not navigate; links appeared to work only because
FLAG_ACTIVITY_CLEAR_TOP against a standard launch mode forced recreation. Now
singleTop with the pending id in observable state, consumed once acted on.

UI

Extracted links were inert text, so the whole URL-extraction stage terminated in
something the user could look at and not use. Now openable.

App icons were rasterised via toBitmap() outside remember, on the main thread,
for every visible card on every frame.

Delete was long-press-only with no label, so a screen-reader user could not
discover or reach it at all.

603 unit tests, 56 instrumented, 0 failures. assembleDebug and lintDebug clean.
